  "query_preview": "..\n\nUpper ridging will guide warm and dry conditions through Friday.\nLook for Friday highs in the 70s and 80s with relative humidity\nbelow 20 percent in the southwest which may elevate fire weather\nconcerns. Light winds or short duration breezy conditions should\nkeep the risk limited.\n\nCold frontal passage remains on schedule for Friday night with\nshowers increasing into Saturday and Saturday night, lingering \ninto Sunday. Some rain may mix with or change to wet snow. \nOverall, little snow accumulation is expected, save for usual \ncolder elevated and grassy surfaces. Wetting rains are also likely\nsouth of Highway 2.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was blended with a nudge from NBM90 for Friday afternoon \nhighs to account for a little compressional warming ahead of the\ncold front. Confidence is increasing on chances for rain and snow\nthis weekend, but remains below average for accumulations given\nthe warm ground temperatures and steadiest QPF amounts remaining\nto the south.",
